# Scripts are LF, in the index and in the working copy.
#
# Not a style preference. A `.mjs` under scripts/ that starts with a shebang
# and has CRLF line endings cannot be imported by a vitest test: it fails with
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, reported against line 4 of the
# *importing* test file, which is a comment.
#
# `src/lib/__tests__/questionStatsBuilder.test.ts` sat broken on main for
# exactly this reason and its whole 17-test suite never ran. A previous
# investigation cleared the test file and was right to: it was byte-identical to
# origin/main, valid UTF-8, and `node --check` passed on both of its imports.
# The problem was in `scripts/knowledge/build-question-stats.mjs`, and the
# reported position was not where it was.
#
# Isolated 2026-09-09 in a clean checkout, one variable at a time. CRLF on the
# test file alone: passes. CRLF on both imports: fails. CRLF on
# build-question-stats.mjs alone: fails. Same file, same CRLF, shebang removed:
# passes. So it is the shebang and the line endings together, and 1,796 CRLF
# files under src/ are unaffected because nothing strips a shebang from them.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `input` here, so git already writes LF on checkout. What
# this adds is that a tool which rewrites a whole file cannot quietly leave CRLF
# behind in a tree git still calls clean. `src/lib/__tests__/lineEndings.test.ts`
# is the guard that speaks up if one appears anyway.
scripts/** text=auto eol=lf
